<title>THAILAND: IFCT sees 7.2 pct Thai GDP growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>IFCT sees 7.2 pct Thai GDP growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Finance Corp of Thailand on Friday said it expected the Thai gross domestic product to expand 7.2 percent in 1997 against a projected 6.8 percent this year.</p>
<p>Following are economic indicators projected by the industrial financing bank:</p>
<p>						   1997	  1996</p>
<p> GDP growth (%)				 7.2	   6.8</p>
<p> Inflation (%)				  4.5	   5.7</p>
<p> Export growth (%)			    9.5	   3.2</p>
<p> Import growth (%)			    8.5	   6.4</p>
<p> Current account deficit (bln baht)     410	   392</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-2529950-3</p>
</text>
